    dct:description "Honda (1971) 3D local orthonormal frame rotation recursion (`_honda_local_frame`, `grow_honda_1971_3d_tree`, L129-261), 4-archetype 3D crown morphospace (L263-292), Honda & Fisher (1978) 5-whorl disk-union effective leaf area functional and 2D (theta_1, theta_2) optimization surface (L294-470) and Leonardo/Shinozaki pipe-model tapering are unchanged from v2 and correct. Pass 3 adds the Campbell & Norman (1998) solar geometry (`solar_elevation_azimuth`, L503-521; day length L524-528), Cooper (1969) declination (L498-500), transmittance-weighted diurnal sun paths (L531-563), a stacked tiered crown (L566-610), tier-to-tier shadow ray tracing with Beer-Lambert tau_c^n (L643-692) and the latitude x spacing sweep (L695-764), backed by 5 Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys). Deductions: the ray-traced crown is a stack of planar disk-union tiers with uniform tau_c, not the 3D Honda internode skeleton (`grow_honda_1971_3d_tree` is never passed to the ray tracer) (-3); direct beam only, no diffuse sky radiance, leaf scattering or penumbra (-2); the 3D builder's pitch factors 0.25*t1 / -0.18*t2 (L221-222) and the daughter-2 extra pi/2 roll (L239) are not in Honda (1971) and are uncited (-2); the tier-order schedule max(2, 5 - 4t//n) (L586) is a modelling choice (-1)." ;
